{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/894620-want-to-develop-a-chrofd-fanfic-idea","id":894620,"title":"Want to develop a ChrofD fanfic idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-20T02:18:48-07:00","id":894620,"title":"Want to develop a ChrofD fanfic idea","content":"Okay, first of all, I really don't know if this is or isn't legal here. If I've broken a rule, please delete this topic and I'll accept my punishment for it.<br /> <br /> So, this is something that's been bugging me a long time, and I finally decided to bite the bullet and ask it here. I've long had an idea for a Chronicles of Darkness/Black Lagoon crossover fic, but the problem is, the basic premise is that, in a once in a millennium event, a freakishly charismatic and forward-thinking Ring of Demons has managed to unite an army of other monsters behind the idea of capturing a significant chunk of land, one already rather detached from the normal laws of the world, and completely severing it from conventional reality to create a literal &quot;Hell&quot; where they can rule openly.<br /> <br /> Naturally, they've chosen Roanapur for various reasons, most of which boil down to &quot;nobody would miss it if it went missing&quot;. So, one fateful day when the stars are right, they muster their forces, unleash occultic occlusion upon the island to temporarily sever it from all communication with the outside world, and then march on Roanapur in full-force. This is a once-in-forever, do or die sort of event, so they're either going to win or lose spectacularly.<br /> <br /> The reason I'm actually going public to talk about this is because, really, I'm just not sure that the twilits would actually stand a chance, and so I was hoping folks might give me their feedback.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's stated outright in the Demon Storyteller's Guide that demonic endgames like &quot;escape to an alternate world/parallel dimension/alternate timeline/whatever&quot; is perfectly legit. So, theoretically, a combination of destroyed/subverted Infrastructure and patronage from one or more Archmages should be able to &quot;break&quot; the island away from Earth proper and transport it Elsewhere to form the nascent seed for a new world. I think.<br /> <br /> What I'm worried about is that whether or not an army of twilit races working in coordination with each other could legitimately conquer even a comparatively small and anarchic human community like Roanapur, or if it'd just come off as too unbelievable that they could inflict any kind of damage to a city at all. The Chronicles of Darkness aren't the World of Darkness, after all; the twilits have had a lot of fangs pulled in comparison, so whether or not they could actually destroy the existing power structure and butcher &amp; intimidate the mortals into bowing before them is... well, I just wanted to know if it would be believably possible.<br /> <br /> If it helps, the army contains a mixture of the &quot;common&quot; splats - vampires, mages, werewolves, changelings - with a minority of sin-eaters (the rarest) and prometheans. There's a handful - about 5 or 6 - mummies, roughly two to three times as many leviathans, and their respective cults. They vary a lot in power level, but average around the equivalent of power stat 2-4; old enough to be disillusioned with humanity/the world as it is, but young enough to still believe that there could be something better out there. And, of course, there's more exceptional types, those who've reached power stat 5 or sometimes even beyond. To say nothing of how the mummies start at power level 10 when woken up. The leadership behind it all is a Ring of three of the Unchained, with perhaps more, lesser level ones serving as &quot;recruits&quot;, and at least one Archmage interested in seeing if this experiment in growing a &quot;new world&quot; could be made to pay off.<br /> <br /> Also, to elaborate on what I had planned as their plan of attack:<br /> Agents of the &quot;Army of Darkness&quot; (for lack of a better placeholder name) have been in Roanapur for months, scouting out its power structures and priority targets, both mundane and supernatural. When a particularly favorable occultic event occurs (&quot;the stars are right&quot;), the army launches its initial strike, using a combination of Leviathan ritualism, Werewolf spirit-invocations and Mage spells to turn Roanapur into a &quot;dead zone&quot;, blocking satellite feeds and all mundane communication. Nobody can see inside, nobody can get any word out.<br /> <br /> At the same time, the existing agents are turned loose to go after specific targets, bolstered by specialists sent in just beforehand to destabilize the situation - assassins go after the major political figures, strike squads attack Infrastructure, loci are seized, etc.<br /> <br /> Then, and only then, does the bulk of the army roll in out of the night to launch its attack. It's open warfare in the streets as monsters fight with police, gangsters, mercenaries, basically anyone stupid enough to get in their way. And even then, this is just a distraction, as the most potent ritualists are deployed to seize the sites necessary to perform their &quot;Great Work&quot; and sunder Roanapur from the rest of the world. If it succeeds, then and only then do they give their demands: surrender, or die.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, the basic presumption here is of the ChrofD standard in that Humans Don't Know. There are people with some vague inkling of the occult underground beneath them, but nowhere near enough that there are people actively trained or prepared en masse to fight against the things that go bump in the night. The big bosses of Roanapur, for example, do have formidable defenses, but that's because they're criminals in a lawless hive of a city; they're expecting to defend themselves against humans, not vampires or a pack of werewolves.<br /> <br /> So... yeah, anyway, I'll admit it's kind of a crazy idea, but still, I'd be interested in at least seeing what happens now I posted this. It would be a pleasant surprise to see if people out there actually agree that, in numbers and united, the twilit races of the ChrofD would be a legitimate danger to humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> For those of you unfamiliar with Black Lagoon and Roanapur, a basic guide to the city would be that... well, probably the nicest thing you can say about the place is that it's a shithole. A lawless island city-state in Thailand's waters, Roanapur is a nexus for every single criminal activity, illegal vice or just plain depravity you can imagine. Black marketing, smuggling, drug trafficking, prostitution, pornography, assassins, mercenaries, human trafficking... you name it, it can be found in Roanapur. It's a city inhabited almost entirely by criminals, the insane, the degenerate and the desperate. Everyone knows that the real power lies in the hand of the cartels, and even then, the true powerhouses of the city are Hotel Moscow (a squadron of Soviet VDV special forces gone renegade and turned into a criminal empire) and the Kan Yi Fan Triad, who constantly jockey for power.<br /> <br /> To give you some idea what kind of hellhole this place is; at one point in its home series, the head of Hotel Moscow contacts the city's premier pornography distributor and asks for a copy of every single item of child pornography or child snuff in his stock featuring Romanian twins (long story, it's to identify a pair of recently arrived psychos). She gets <b>two hundred and fifty individual tapes</b>, and later she and the head of the Kan Yi Fan admit to being a little disgusted at the revelation.<br /> <br /> Frankly, being conquered and/or razed to the ground by an army of rampaging monsters would probably be a step UP for this place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T03:02:47-07:00","id":894639,"title":"","content":"Legality, no idea.<br /> <br /> Could it be done? With the power levels of the guys you've mentioned as being part of the &quot;Army of Darkness&quot;, definitely. A Gnosis five mastigos can't really lose to a fight against mortals when he's the one picking the fight.<br /> <br /> My main questions though, how in the heck did a ring of three demons manage to get this sort of group together. Four or Five mummies, an archmaster, dozens of less powerful, yet still exceptionally powerful supernatural monster working together? For example, the idea of an Archmaster joining to see if a pocket reality could be formed? Don't Archmasters have to do this permanently to stop themselves being torn apart by the energies of the Supernal?<br /> <br /> I don't think it's a terrible idea or anything, but you might be better off expanding the demons ring and their allies/contacts and having them be a group trying to do this. The supernatural coalition thing is fun, but at least relying on the WoD setting material, it seems extremely unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T04:28:05-07:00","id":894657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/894620-want-to-develop-a-chrofd-fanfic-idea#post894620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this is something that's been bugging me a long time, and I finally decided to bite the bullet and ask it here. I've long had an idea for a Chronicles of Darkness/Black Lagoon crossover fic, but the problem is, the basic premise is that, in a once in a millennium event, a freakishly charismatic and forward-thinking Ring of Demons has managed to unite an army of other monsters behind the idea of capturing a significant chunk of land, one already rather detached from the normal laws of the world, and completely severing it from conventional reality to create a literal &quot;Hell&quot; where they can rule openly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. This pretty much parallels a project of my own I am working on (though that was further back in time, comprised solely of Demons, and was successful, for certain values of success). Hopefully I'll have enough material to post soon. I'm interested in seeing where this goes.<br /> <br /> What about the established supernatural presence in Roanapur? Did the Army of Darkness recruit <i>all</i> of the natives?<br /> <br /> What is the primary goal for this? Setting material? Platform for (short) stories? Is the event what is focused on, or the aftermath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T05:50:19-07:00","id":894673,"title":"","content":"As far as i am Aware (Not great on the Legality of it 100%) Fanfics and Fan-Projects usually fall under Fair use. Aslong as you are not making a profit off of it generally it's fine (Don't quote me on that.. but that seems to be the general rule) Also depends on the Company... Onyx Path seem to be fine with Fan Projects aslong as it's not literally reposting Wholesale the Books and pieces of them. (Quoting parts of it for Reference I believe is fine, But Posting entire Chapters? Nope.)<br /> <br /> Otherwise it might be interesting too read/look into. I'll keep an Eye out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T09:52:35-07:00","id":894776,"title":"","content":"...Wow. First of all, let me thank you all for surprising me with your amazingly non-hostile reactions. I would quote those of you whom I'm replying to, but my connection absolutely hates whatever this forum is running on, so I can't do that.<br /> <br /> @Gullinbursti:<br /> To be honest, I don't particularly want to go as high as the &quot;Overlords tier&quot; - the Archmages and their ilk - because, even in my headcanon, they usually have far better things to do than to directly pay attention to the works of mortals as a whole, and even lesser supernaturals. I just didn't know if they had a hope of pulling off something like this without a &quot;Prime Mover&quot; covertly supporting them from the Supernal.<br /> <br /> I don't think I quite follow what you're saying with that last line, but I'm going to stick with the crossover/coalition approach to this. It's the true part that excites me about this whole thing; seeing what all of monsterdom could do if they were willing to get off of their asses and work together. It does need a lot of work and a bit of handwaving to pull off, but I think it can be done. It's not like this is canonical in anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Vent0:<br /> Thank you. As the opening post hopefully conveyed, I really want to keep the suspension of disbelief bar from being too high, so any advice or discussions about making their efforts believable would be greatly appreciated. Even with Gullinbursti's hope-inspiring comment about how monsters have a lot more &quot;punch&quot; when they're the ones picking the fight, I don't really want to be on the losing side of a debate like &quot;Hotel Moscow should easily weather and defeat a surprise attack by five Blood Potency 5 vampires, each with at least mastery (Discipline value 5) of their Clan Disciplines&quot;.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to reply to your questions:<br /> <br /> Now that you've mentioned the supernatural presence for Roanapur, I figure that it's mostly comprised of vampires, werewolves and mages. As I covered in brief in my opening post, this is an anarchic, unstable, vice-ruled place. Not the sort of place where many of the ChrofD's twilit-folk would be attracted to living - can you see a changeling staying sane in a place with daily gun battles? Hell, if a mummy lived there, the place would probably be <b>gone</b> already, as a result of people being dumb enough to steal her Relics.<br /> <br /> Vampires are a mixture of clans; there's a heavy Belial's Brood presence here, and it's lawless enough that they're roughly tolerated as genuine equals, though the non-converts (mostly Unaligned and perhaps a handful of Ordo Dracul and Croneites) stay away. They form the largest supernatural presence here, as Roanapur is a place where blood flows like water and there's plenty of easily-drained prey to be had. As a whole, they're onboard with the invasion; Roanapur is too anarchic a place for them to really control from the shadows, and if there was a ever a place to stir their desires of ruling openly, it's Roanapur.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are... in a lot of trouble. Roanapur is either one <b>giant</b> Wound (which is why there's a fairly sizable amount of Uratha in the &quot;Army&quot;; getting rid of a spiritual sinkhole like this is a win-win for everybody), or else it's such a shithole that it's the kind of place where spirits of Murder, Rape, Drug Addiction, Prostitution, Lust, etc can thrive without the direct influence of the Maeljin (assuming those still exist in the Idigam Chronicles). Either way, there's a beleaguered minority of Uratha desperately struggling to try and make some kind of change, who're so overwhelmed that they welcome the outside help, and a presence of Bale Hounds - mostly working to undo the works of the former or to give the Maeljin more of an &quot;in&quot; with the local Choirs. Still, in either case, there's not a huge presence of them, mostly because Roanapur is A: such a shithole, and B: such an effectively self-sustaining shithole. It doesn't need a large amount of werewolf &quot;coaxing&quot; to stay a place of evil.<br /> <br /> Mages are definitely the minority of native supernaturals; Roanapur isn't the sort of place conducive to Awakenings. Most of them probably leave the city, if not quite so drivenly as sin-eaters (think about it; Roanapur is the kind of place where getting shot either deliberately or by accident at your local bar is just one of the acceptable risks; do you wanna think about how bad it must be for Sin-Eater to hang out here?). Definitely not in any real position to object to some outside &quot;cleanup&quot;.<br /> <br /> Primary goal for this is, I would probably say, &quot;platform for short(?) stories&quot;. I am curious how you think it'd work as &quot;setting material&quot;, though?<br /> <br /> Focus is definitely on the event proper. That's the big thing here, the whole &quot;night of blood and ichor&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> @RickmanUK:<br /> \u200bThank you so much for the words of encouragement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:31:06-07:00","id":894804,"title":"","content":"I'm really curious about the rules of CofD fanfic now. Because fanfic is generally a border-case; there's arguments that it's fair use, and arguments that it's copyright infringement. The majority of author/creator-run boards have basically a DADT policy: write what you want on your own time, but if you post it, they have to take it down and tell you not to do it, because they need to defend their copyright. It's fine if it exists, but the author/creator has to have plausible deniability.<br /> <br /> Except with RPGs, the whole <i>point</i> of the thing is to have people creating their own stories in this world, and there's plenty of &quot;pitch your campaign&quot; or &quot;share your stories&quot; or &quot;how does this work in your version&quot; threads, and that sort of thing is fine. So I'd guess as long as you're not planning to sell it, it's okay? <br /> <br /> That said, in terms of your &quot;does this suspend disbelief&quot; question, I'm a little confused as to which supernaturals are where. Initially, it sounded like you had a small group taking over a town, and I can see 10 or so supernaturals rolling a town of mortals. But then you say &quot;army,&quot; and I've got no idea how big that is; assuming &quot;5-6 Mummies&quot; is one of the median numbers, that implies over a hundred in this army, and yeah, they can definitely roll a town, even with a number of other supernatural groups who would oppose them (as long as they strike first and fast, which you have them doing. Whether or not they hold the town, that's a different problem.) Honestly I think the archmaster angle throws it in the opposite direction; having someone like that involved seems more unbelievable than your army taking the town. (That and I disagree about your Mage/Sin-Eater numbers; stress and strife cause Awakenings, and more deaths = more people willing to make a deal to not be dead.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T10:51:53-07:00","id":894824,"title":"","content":"Yes, as I said in my last post, I'm probably going to dump the idea of there being an Archmage involved.<br /> <br /> As for the Mages &amp; Sin-Eaters of Roanapur, basically, what I'm seeing is this:<br /> <br /> Firstly, in a cynical, soul-crushing environment like Roanapur, few Mages would Awaken, and fewer still of those would stay. You can do anything now, and you want to hang out in Southeast Asia's garbage dump?<br /> <br /> Secondly, not only is Sin-Eating harder to do than just &quot;die&quot; (plus, keep in mind that a Sin-Eater only comes back if A: the brain isn't destroyed, and B: the body isn't too mutilated - Roanapur is filled with so many vicious, professional thugs that it has &quot;Cleaners&quot; like Sawyer who specialise in chopping up bodies to get rid of them), they would be far less likely to stick around than Mages. Reason why? Remember what the corebook says is the Inherently Sucky Thing about being a Sin-Eater? The whole &quot;I can hear the dead... and they won't shut up!&quot; angle. Living in Roanapur means getting screamed at by legions of angry, vengeful ghosts day-in, day-out.<br /> <br /> But... I could be wrong. If this topic isn't likely to get me smacked with the banhammer any time soon, then I don't mind discussing this kind of thing. I'm still trying to refine it down from what I want to do, after getting over the initial hurdle of &quot;can monsters in numbers really pose a threat to humans in numbers?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:50:00-07:00","id":894859,"title":"","content":"Well, in terms of banhammers, so far so good, right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I guess I take an opposite view on Awakenings: if there's lots of stress and strife, someone's more likely to see through the Lie (since there must be something more, the world can't be like this, the world shouldn't be like this), whereas if someone's happy and safe, they have much less incentive for Awakening. They may not stick around, but depending on what Mystery caught their attention (particularly if it's related to why their home is so terrible), there's mystical reasons for them to stay, not to mention the human ones. <br /> <br /> I also don't see Sin-Eaters exiting as quickly as they crop up. Yeah, it's a deadly place, but that whole &quot;come back from the dead&quot; trick is only necessary if you, y'know, die. If a Sin-Eater gets clipped, they can heal themselves enough to stay alive (particularly if this was a non-targetted attack). Plus, all those ghosts must know a lot of hiding places, which is gonna help. And again, more bodies = more Sin-Eaters, statistically. <br /> <br /> I don't know the setting any more than what you've said, but I like the Vampire and Werewolf status quos, they make sense. I might attribute some of the permanent unhappiness to a Promethean's Wasteland, too (if you wanted to go that route). In terms of the locals, even hives of scum and villainy learn that some people aren't to be messed with (your theoretical Mummy, after destroying ten thieves, would probably be left in relative peace). I don't think such a place would drive out Changelings, per se; bad things happen, and in some cases, Arcadia was worse. At least here, you don't have the police breathing down your back, wondering why you don't exist. Any Beasts in the area? This seems like a great place for whatever Hunger they have: lots of stuff to take, people to beat, stuff to destroy, and all pretty guilt-free, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5695-aceofalmonds","name":"AceOfAlmonds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5695_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"323"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T11:51:37-07:00","id":894861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/894620-want-to-develop-a-chrofd-fanfic-idea?p=894824#post894824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;I can hear the dead... and they won't shut up!&quot; angle. Living in Roanapur means getting screamed at by legions of angry, vengeful ghosts day-in, day-out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there are that many ghosts floating around, why aren't they causing trouble? Did they but to locals know how to counter them? Does something prevent them from doing so anyways? Is something <i>eating</i> them?<br /> <br /> That's just one case where we can look at the circumstances, draw conclusions... and wonder why something isn't the case when it <i>should</i> be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/894620-want-to-develop-a-chrofd-fanfic-idea?p=894824#post894824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But... I could be wrong. If this topic isn't likely to get me smacked with the banhammer any time soon, then I don't mind discussing this kind of thing. I'm still trying to refine it down from what I want to do, after getting over the initial hurdle of &quot;can monsters in numbers really pose a threat to humans in numbers?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Monsters in <i>small</i> numbers can roll over large amounts of humans. It depends on numerous factors, of course. Who initiating hostilities has the advantage of knowing when the attack will occur, and in what arena. How gullible are the targets or aggressors? Are any counter-measures or precautions in place?<br /> <br /> For example, the hardest, most ruthless warlord with a trained, well equipped army can't do squat against target that can scout them out from Twilight or snipe them from across the Gauntlet. An army trained to obey orders without question is in a hard spot when a vampire can just mind control their superior and get the whole force for the price of one pawn.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if a group of monsters rolls in and expects the &quot;simple mortals&quot; can't stand against their power, only to find themselves faced with a fortified group of Hunters, wielding their Banes, knowing how to avoid or minimize their abilities, and countering their influence - bad times for said monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T12:41:31-07:00","id":894910,"title":"","content":"Your legality is fine, as far as I'm aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T13:55:26-07:00","id":894973,"title":"","content":"@ArcaneArts:<br /> Thanks for the head's up. I'll stop worrying about that now.<br /> <br /> <br /> @AceofAlmonds:<br /> Only problem with that is that, isn't &quot;make the world a shitty place, to keep the Awakenings down&quot; explicitly called out as one of the things that the Seers do to enforce the Lie? So, wouldn't Roanapur be the kind of Lie-entrapping pit that the Exarches would like? That said, you may be right, and I may be underestimating the sheer number of Mages in the city.<br /> <br /> For Sin-Eaters, the problem is that making the <i>initial pact</i> requires dying in a manner that they can be successfully revived from, which, as far as I remember, means &quot;no bullets in the head and no bodily dismemberment&quot;... in a town of criminals, where execution typically entails being shot in the head and then delivered to a Cleaner to be cut into pieces for easy disposal. Or just being chopped up whilst you live, depending on who you pissed off. I admit I may be overthinking the matter again.<br /> <br /> As for low Changeling numbers, the reason I figured they were basically a non-entity is because of how chaotic Roanapur is with how harsh the 1e Clarity meter was. By RAW, a changeling living in a place with multiple daily gun fights, random shootouts, and murders is probably going to drop down to about Clarity 3 at best in pretty short order. I admit I don't know if the 2e revamp for Clarity is out yet, and I have toyed with revamping it more than once, but I just figured Roanapur is too sanity-grating for any Changelings to stay.<br /> <br /> I probably wouldn't go with the Wasteland effect, seeing as how that tends to lead to a lot of physical degradation as well. You're right in that the city's practically a Mecca for Prometheans on the Refinement of Cobalus, though.<br /> <br /> Beasts... in all honesty, I haven't been able to get into Beasts. I tried, especially after the initial reveals of it in development back in 2015 had me so excited, but, I just can't wrap my head around them. I'm probably going to leave them out of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> @Vent0:<br /> Well, the most obvious answer is that Roanapur isn't set in the Chronicles of Darkness, but that's boring. :P That is something that needs figuring out. I suppose the most obvious/vanilla answer is that the city's resident overworked Moros and Sin-Eaters struggle to keep them underwraps, and what gets through tends to just be dismissed as part of the endless stream of overuses, shootings, stabbings and other casual deaths that are so endemic in the most lawless place on earth.<br /> <br /> The targets are... well, I would definitely not call them gullible, for the most part. It varies. The Columbian Cartel and the Scilian Mafia, canonically, are kind of the &quot;dumb muscle&quot; of the four major powers; they survive mostly through having just enough smarts to not push Hotel Moscow or the Kan Yi Fan too far with their posturing and with having plenty of manpower to flood the streets. Hotel Moscow and Kan Yi Fan are the &quot;elites&quot;; smart, well-trained, disciplined, ruthless and well-armed. But they don't know that there's monsters out there, and they don't have any truck with the supernatural themselves. There's no vampires manipulating the gangs, no mages on the payroll (that they know of, anyway), and they aren't expecting to ever fight creatures of the night.<br /> <br /> The aggressors, though, are smart; they've had agents inside getting feedback on how Roanapur works, who's in charge, how they work, and they're not to expecting to just march into the streets and have mortals surrender. I admit I haven't thought too hard beyond that.<br /> <br /> One of the things I did think hard about was a decapitating strike at Hotel Moscow. The &quot;Bloodgods&quot;, for lack of a better placeholder name, are a band of five powerful vampire assassins set on the Mafiya outpost after dusk has set. Fully tanked with blood, their goal is simple: use their powers to assault the Hotel and kill as many of its upper agents as possible, with a focus on taking down their leader, Balalaika. The Mafiya are armed and watchful, but they're not specifically expecting anyone to directly attack them, nor do they have anti-vampire tech.<br /> <br /> I don't know if they'd have a chance of succeeding or not. Big issue is, if I'm going to write this, I need to balance &quot;what's the smart thing to do&quot; with &quot;what will people actually enjoy reading&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-20T15:41:11-07:00","id":895052,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, people still Awaken in shit-holes like Roanapur, but they do so for different reasons. The sheer suffering and desperation might cause an overabundance of Mastigos Awakenings, for example. And these Mages would not be as organized or interested in Mysteries as those in more developed countries. I'm certain they'd be more interested in escaping, like you pointed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:04:57-07:00","id":897097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/894620-want-to-develop-a-chrofd-fanfic-idea?p=895052#post895052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, people still Awaken in shit-holes like Roanapur, but they do so for different reasons. The sheer suffering and desperation might cause an overabundance of Mastigos Awakenings, for example. And these Mages would not be as organized or interested in Mysteries as those in more developed countries. I'm certain they'd be more interested in escaping, like you pointed out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Moros Awakenings from people with near-death experiences, or Thyrsus ones that arise from predator-prey narratives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:58:11-07:00","id":897155,"title":"","content":"So... I'm not really sure what else to talk about for this now. Now that the whole &quot;cowering in fear that this is going to get me banned&quot; stuff is sorted out and done with, I'm at a loss how to continue with actually developing this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:06:12-07:00","id":897162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/894620-want-to-develop-a-chrofd-fanfic-idea?p=897155#post897155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... I'm not really sure what else to talk about for this now. Now that the whole &quot;cowering in fear that this is going to get me banned&quot; stuff is sorted out and done with, I'm at a loss how to continue with actually developing this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think about what stories or scenes stand out in your mind that made you want to write this. Start from there, working forward or backward as needed. Add more stories that tie into those, either directly or tangently. Then looks for conceptual or thematic holes you missed with the previous stories. Or stories that patch over the &quot;Wait why didn't...&quot; questions from previous ones.<br /> <br /> But start with what interested you to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}